// White items: ED and res tags go on the tag line with the staffmods, in the game's order (S14 descpriority: skill
// tabs 151, enhanced damage 129-130, single skills 81, enhanced defense 74, resistances 34-40). A later rule puts its
// tag further left, so: res and enhanced defense here, the single skills below, enhanced damage and the Amazon skill
// tabs at the end. The ** markers stay on the name line (220). BH gives a white item one line break (superior, or
// with staffmods or automods).
ItemDisplay[NMAG !RW !INF ((DIN RES>4) OR (SUP ED>4 !SOCK=1 (CHEST OR HELM OR SHIELD OR WEAPON)))]:%CL%%NAME%{%NAME%}%CONTINUE%

// Label All Res Paladin shields when leveling
ItemDisplay[NMAG !INF !RW RES>4 DIN]:%WHITE%%RES%%PURPLE%res%CS%%NAME%{%NAME%}%CONTINUE%//

// Enhanced Defense Armors
ItemDisplay[(CHEST OR HELM OR SHIELD) !SOCK=1 !INF SUP NMAG !RW ED~5-13]:%WHITE%%ED%%LIGHT_GRAY%ed%CS%%NAME%{%NAME%}%CONTINUE%//
ItemDisplay[(CHEST OR HELM OR SHIELD) !SOCK=1 !INF SUP NMAG !RW ED>13]:%WHITE%%ED%%BLUE%ed%CS%%NAME%{%NAME%}%CONTINUE%//

// Show staffmods on NMAG items


// Daggers
ItemDisplay[NMAG !RW CLVL>79 DAGGER !THROWING !(SK73>2 OR SK254>2 OR SK257>2 OR SK259>2 OR SK265>2 OR SK266>2 OR SK269>2 OR SK270>2 OR SK274>2 OR SK275>2 OR SK280>2) FILTLVL>0 !TOWN]:// Hides daggers that don't have +3 to a skill past level 80
